<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Opoku Ware I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1720–<a href="/years/1750">1750</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Opoku Ware I was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asantehene">Asantehene</a>, or ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>, from about 1720 to 1750, succeeding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osei-tutu-i">Osei Tutu</a>. His campaigns greatly expanded the empire's territory. Accounts of the Ashanti Empire note that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> observers reported Asante armies of 50,000 men in the field during his campaigns.</p></div>
